{% comment %}
  Which colour does a material value name?

  Cullinan (2026-10-03). The colour row is not drawn on a product page; the material
  stands for the colour instead, so every material value has to say which colour it
  is. This is the one place that decides it, for the picker, the options snippet and
  the cart (product-twin-option.liquid, product-variant-options.liquid).

  A colour is named when its name, lower-cased, sits inside the material value's name,
  lower-cased ("жълто злато" inside "14К жълто злато", "сребро" inside "925 сребро").
  Where a value names several the longest name wins, so "жълто злато" beats "злато".
  English "silver" is read as "сребро" on both sides: the Admin of this store mixes the
  two (a bracelet whose material says "Silver" next to a colour called "Сребро"), and
  a pair that differs only in language must not be left unpaired -- or paired with
  whichever colour happens to come first, which would put a rose-gold colour on a
  silver order.

  Prints the colour value's own name (exactly as the Admin has it) or nothing.

  Accepts:
  - colour_option: {Object} the hidden colour option (a product_option with swatches).
  - material_name: {String} the name of the material value.

  Usage:
  {%- capture twin_name -%}
    {%- render 'product-twin-match', colour_option: twin, material_name: value.name -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign material_down = material_name | downcase | replace: 'silver', 'сребро'
  assign best_length = 0
  assign best_name = ''

  for colour_value in colour_option.values
    assign colour_down = colour_value.name | downcase | replace: 'silver', 'сребро'
    if colour_down != blank and material_down contains colour_down
      assign colour_length = colour_down | size
      if colour_length > best_length
        assign best_name = colour_value.name
        assign best_length = colour_length
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  echo best_name
-%}
